  "Question": "Ray OA rotates about its endpoint O. When the terminal side first forms a straight line with the initial side, the angle formed is called a",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "Right angle",
    "B": "Straight angle",
    "C": "Full angle",
    "D": "Obtuse angle"
  },
  "Correct Answer": "B",
  "Accepted Answers": [],
  "Unordered Answers": false,
  "Solution": "The angle formed when the terminal side and initial side form a straight line is a straight angle (\\(180^\\circ\\)). Continuing the rotation until the terminal side coincides with the initial side forms a full angle.",
